course: dictionary
lesson: 5657
title: Literacy: reading, writing and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Literacy is the ability to read and write. At school, «literacy lessons» are the lessons where you practise reading stories and writing your own.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. Literacy can mean knowledge and skill in a certain area, such as computer literacy, money literacy or media literacy. The words around it give the clue: if the sentence names a subject, literacy means being skilled in it.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Then in literacy Grace reads out a story about a dinosaur who opens a bakery — Lily's idea, from Tuesday.» Literacy comes before reading out a story, so here it means the reading and writing lesson.
fact: Literacy means the ability to read and write.
fact: Literacy can also mean knowledge and skill in a certain area, such as computer literacy or money literacy.
fact: Media literacy helps you spot fake news.
fact: World Literacy Day is a special day about reading and writing, and some charities teach adults to read.
fact: «Literacy lessons» (UK) are lessons for reading and writing.
exercise: «Then in literacy Grace reads out a story about a dinosaur who opens a bakery.» What is literacy here? | A story about a dinosaur | A bakery where dinosaurs work | A day of the week | *A lesson for reading and writing
exercise: Ella says media literacy helps you spot fake news. What is media literacy? | *A skill that helps you judge what you see and read in the media | A type of camera | The ability to draw a map | A TV channel for children
exercise: Find the word that means the ability to read and write. | bakery | Tuesday | story | *literacy
test: What does computer literacy mean? | Playing computer games all day | Being able to fix a bicycle | *Knowledge and skill with computers | A computer shop
test: Which of these is a literacy lesson? | A maths test | A PE lesson in the park | Cooking pasta in a kitchen | *Reading a story and writing about it in class
exam: Mia says, «Money literacy helps me save.» What does money literacy mean? | *Knowing how to manage money well | Being able to count coins only | Money made from paper | A bank that sells books
